cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SVengers: a multi-evidence germline CNV caller with calibrated post-calling filtering"
message: "If you use SVengers, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mathieu
    given-names: Alexandre
    affiliation: "Institut Pasteur, GHFC lab"
    email: alexandre.mathieu@pasteur.fr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3418-9425"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bourgeron-lab/SVengers"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24308195
abstract: >-
  SVengers calls germline deletions and duplications from short-read whole-genome
  sequencing by combining read depth, discordant pairs, split reads and B-allele
  frequency, scores every call with a calibrated gradient-boosting model trained
  partly on genomes with coverage waves, and joins family and cohort samples with
  forced genotyping, cohort filters and pedigree annotation (inheritance, confirmed
  de novo calls). Version 2.1 is the method frozen for its publication.
keywords:
  - CNV
  - structural variants
  - WGS
  - bioinformatics
version: 2.1.6
date-released: 2026-11-23
